# Lockeroom Database — Architecture & Business Rules

This repo connects to the Lockeroom Supabase database. Always refer to `architecture.md` for the full schema reference. Below is a fast-load summary of the most critical rules.

---

## Database

- **Provider:** Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- **Project ID:** `dvrhazdtbsttzduaedzu`
- **Source of truth:** `architecture.md` in this repo

---

## Core Tables (quick ref)

| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `member_database` | Member demographics and primary coach assignment |
| `member_memberships` | One row per membership term — central operational table |
| `member_newsale_metadata` | Financial snapshot for new sales |
| `member_renewal_meta` | Financial snapshot for renewals |
| `member_not_renewing` | Churn tracking — who's leaving and why |
| `member_holds` | Membership pauses |
| `member_daily_sessions_attended` | Actual session attendance |
| `member_lcns` | Late cancels and no-shows |
| `staff_database` | All staff, coaches, and roles. `staff_bio` + `avatar_path` (added 2026-07-07) are the canonical public profile fields exposed to LR Member App members via `get_staff_directory` only. |
| `work_estimations` | Per-client hour allocations per role |
| `system_config` | Session durations and contract hour baselines |
| `membership_types` | Membership product definitions |
| `membership_versions` | Historical pricing and policy snapshots |
| `member_physicals_raw` | Physical assessment data — movement screen, benchmarks, focus/avoid fields. One row per assessment. |
| `member_health_metrics` | Body composition (InBody + ingest). Live columns: `bfm`, `ffm`, `smm`, `bone_mineral_content`, `tbw`, `bmr`, `age`, `inbody_score`, `source`. See `architecture.md` §12. |
| `member_nutrition_targets` | Coach-managed current calorie/macro targets — one row per member. Member app read-only; Coach OS writes via service role. See `architecture.md` §12. |
| `member_checkins` | Weekly member wellbeing submissions (wide legacy columns). Dynamic form: `checkin_questions`, `member_checkin_responses`, `resolve_member_checkin_questions`. |
| `member_coach_notes` | Coach notes; member app reads latest `goal` / `habits` via `get_member_current_goal_habit` only. |
| `member_health_activity_daily` | Steps/movement summaries by day. Use `input_kind`: `vendor_daily` vs `manual_checkin_weekly_avg` (member_checkins weekly average — label in UI). Not workouts. |
| `member_health_workouts` | Discrete workout sessions (TeamBuilder, app, Terra `activity`). |
| `member_health_connections` | Maps `member_id` to vendor health accounts (e.g. Terra `user_id`, `reference_id`, `provider`). |
| `member_tbresults` | TeamBuilder raw lift logs — strength pipeline input. |
| `exercise_library` | Exercise → `reporting_pattern`, `coefficient` (fraction of pattern benchmark), `per_limb`, `is_bodyweight`. |
| `member_st_tracker_lifts` | Benchmark metadata only (manual coach rows kept); **not used by metrics math**. |
| `member_st_metrics_daily` | Daily strength aggregates per member/pattern (pattern e-max smoothed, IV volume, tonnage, heavy sets). |
| `member_workout_history_sessions` | Permanent completed-strength workout snapshots across Member App, floor, and TeamBuildr. |
| `member_workout_history_sets` | Permanent set facts and note snapshots for canonical workout sessions. |
| `member_workout_exercise_daily` | Incremental member/exercise/day summaries derived from canonical sets. |

**Strength model (2026-06-10):** UI headline = smoothed **raw** e-max of window’s most-trained lift (no coefficient), computed on-the-fly; `st_pattern_top_exercise_series` for detail chart. `member_st_metrics_daily` still stores coefficient-indexed pattern e-max for IV/heavy baselines. `calculate_e_max` NULL when reps > 12. Sufficiency = ≥3 days on chosen top exercise. `calculate_pattern_state` returns `top_exercise_name` + `sessions_in_window`. No auto-assign cron. See `architecture.md` §13.

**Canonical workout history (2026-07-14):** completed strength only. Member App/floor sessions require a confirmed set and exclude auto-completion; TeamBuildr groups by `(member_id, completed_date)`. Program/title/set/note fields are snapshots and survive source-program deletion. App roles have member-scoped `SELECT` only; use the completion/projector functions for writes. See `architecture.md` §15.

